In article <JBW.93Jan28235109@bigbird.bu.edu> jbw@bigbird.bu.edu (Joe Wells) writes:
>1. How do you specify which window interface to use dynamically?  I have
>   to resort to editing the binary to switch between "tty" and "X11".

If you compile with BOTH the TTY{OBJS,SRCS,LIBS} and the X11{OBJS,SRCS,LIBS}
linked in, then you can switch between them just by changing the
{NETHACK}OPTIONS=windowtype:
in your NETHACKOPTIONS/.nethackrc or the shell variable.  For everyone using
the X11 version, you must move the nethack.rc from win/X11 into ~/.nethackrc
and recompile with the #ifdef TEXTCOLOR enabled in unixconf.h to get the full
effect.  This gets you full use of the cool font, in color no less.

My complaint is that the Makefile insists on doing a full recompile almost
every time.  Yargh....

